{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Come now</b> — with a heh, for there are four standards, and the mixed multitude goes after them like a tail." "<b>Curse for me</b> — his mouth disabled him, for in the end he cursed him." "<b>ברוך</b> — three times in the Masorah: אשר תברך מברך, and the other: יהי שם ה' מבורך, and the other: in Job. This teaches that he knew how to pinpoint the hour in which the Holy One, blessed be He, is angry, and he would curse and bless with it, and this is יהי שם ה' מבורך." "<b>תאור</b> — three times in the Masorah: ואשר תאור, לא תאור את העם, ונשיא בעמך לא תאור. And we derive from it in Sanhedrin: the same applies to every person — therefore לא תאור, that it is forbidden to curse any person." "<b>ואשר תאר יואר</b> — in gematria: שקיללתה את מואב."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:50.919286973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}